{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/394441-do-pacts-have-to-be-something-the-demon-can-do-merit-bumps-aside","id":394441,"title":"do pacts have to be something the demon can do? (merit bumps aside)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-05T21:45:08-08:00","id":394441,"title":"do pacts have to be something the demon can do? (merit bumps aside)","content":"For example, a PCs (we're actually playing Hunter not Demon) wife was murder, suppose he wanted the Demon to bring her back, would the Demon have to possess &quot;Raise Dead&quot; to do this? Another scenario I thought about was information on the whereabouts of the killer. Does the demon have to have a way to learn this information? would it mystically come to her , or the PCs if she signed the deal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T23:17:24-08:00","id":394537,"title":"","content":"If the trait is not represented by a condition which the Demon could remove (such as a debilitating disease), a merit (such as resources representing sudden wealth), or a skill bonus (such as taking a bonus to expression to represent sudden mastery of the guitar) then a Demon has to have the ability to fulfill the bargain. In this case to bring a dead character back to life the demon must be able to do so via their abilities in some way.<br /> <br /> Note, at least in the short term, a demon could possess an ability to do this. There are at least two exploits that can redirect the harm in any event elsewhere, including a death blow. So if the demon is on the scene when the death occurs this could be fixed. There is also, of course, Raise Dead itself.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 02-06-2015, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T02:20:05-08:00","id":394629,"title":"","content":"There is the little blurb on page 192 of the core book that implies that at least with some things the demon doesn't technically have to be able to hold up their end of the bargain.<br /> Granted if I was the ST I would draw limits at how much a PC can expect the pact to do on its own, and probably point out that if the pact fulfills itself it will happen without regard to the demon and its plans. This would also only work for things deemed within the realm of normal probability. For example, a person wants to win the lottery and makes a pact. The possibility existed already for the person to win the lottery and the pact just raises those odds to near certainty. (Interference from other supernatural entities might prevent it from working.) So I wouldn't require a PC's demon to be able to rig the lottery. Your raise the dead example though I would rule the PC would have to be able to do it since the dead don't normally come back to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T03:50:46-08:00","id":394649,"title":"","content":"Well Nalak42, from a mechanical standpoint, you'd be awarding the mortal beneficiary of the pact with dots in the Resources merit. Therefore the lottery would be won to fluff that sudden change in living circumstances to reflect the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T09:14:27-08:00","id":394979,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can. You can work it up so there's at least enough Cover XP you get out of the pact that you could buy a new Cover.<br /> <br /> A Cover that looks and sounds just like that poor fool's wife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T17:06:22-08:00","id":395631,"title":"","content":"I thought building a cover had to have it's traits composed from existing people... also I suspect from these answers that my second question about getting &quot;information&quot; means that the demon would have to have a method of getting said information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:21:12-08:00","id":410495,"title":"","content":"Technically? Yes. But that doesn't mean an enterprising demon wouldn't be able to take care of that with the right knowledge.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.cantstopthemovies.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/10/the-truman-show-perfect-woman-.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Once you've figured out the appearance it's just a matter of using the right Embeds or Exploits. Like Associate &amp; Integrate or Force Relationship.<br /> <br /> And any Demon with Trivia can learn anything it wants at any time, since, you know, &quot;they put everything on the internet nowadays.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:23:58-08:00","id":410593,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that if the Demon applies the trait &quot;married to&quot; and &quot;in love with&quot; as relationships to his or her Cover, giving the person what they wanted but their wish is granted through a mirror darkly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}